“Probes in Kubernetes are health-check mechanisms used by kubelet to monitor container health and availability.

There are mainly three probes:
Liveness Probe
Used to check whether application is alive.
If it fails, Kubernetes restarts the container automatically.
once it cross the threshold reaches it will re-create container

Readiness Probe
Used to check whether application is ready to accept traffic.
If it fails, pod is removed from service endpoints but container is not restarted.

Startup Probe
Used for slow-starting applications to prevent premature restarts during startup phase.

Probes help achieve self-healing, high availability, and zero-downtime deployments in production Kubernetes environments.”

1. Liveness Probe

Checks whether the application is still alive.

If liveness probe fails:
Kubernetes restarts the container
Liveness probe detects this and restarts the container automatically.

Example
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /health
    port: 8080

  initialDelaySeconds: 30
  periodSeconds: 10
  timeoutSeconds: 5
  failureThreshold: 3

Kubernetes checks:
http://pod-ip:8080/health


2.Readiness Probe
Checks whether the application is ready to serve traffic.
If readiness probe fails:
Pod is removed from Service endpoints
BUT:  Container is NOT restarted

Example
readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /ready
    port: 8080

  initialDelaySeconds: 5
  periodSeconds: 3

----------------------------------------------------------------
Important Difference
Probe	What Happens on Failure
Liveness	   Container restarted
Readiness	   Traffic stopped and removed from Service endpoints
-----------------------------------------------------------------
3.Startup Probe
Used for slow-starting applications.

Example
startupProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /startup
    port: 8080

  failureThreshold: 30
  periodSeconds: 10

Meaning:
Application gets 300 seconds to start
--------------------------------------------------
Real Production Example
A common production setup:

Readiness Probe
→ controls traffic

Liveness Probe
→ handles stuck/crashed apps

Startup Probe
→ protects slow-starting apps
------------------------------------------------
Simple Visualization
********************
Container Starts
       ↓
Startup Probe
       ↓
Readiness Probe
       ↓
Traffic Starts
       ↓
Liveness Probe monitors continuously

